{"sections":[],"metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"OUDSTextInput","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"OUDSTextInput","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"struct","platforms":[{"beta":false,"name":"iOS","deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"15.0","unavailable":false},{"introducedAt":"13.0","name":"macOS","deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"beta":false},{"introducedAt":"1.0","name":"visionOS","deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"beta":false}],"modules":[{"name":"Components"}],"title":"OUDSTextInput","externalID":"s:14OUDSComponents13OUDSTextInputV"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Text input is a UI element that allows to enter, edit, or select single-line textual data."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Text input is one of the most fundamental form elements used to capture user input such as names, emails, passwords, or search queries."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"It provides a visual and interactive affordance for text entry while supporting labels, placeholders, icons, descriptions, and validation feedback."}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSTextInput"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@","kind":"attribute"},{"text":"MainActor","preciseIdentifier":"s:ScM","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"OUDSTextInput","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"mentions","mentions":["doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/Controls"]},{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"Layout","level":2,"text":"Layout"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Text input is based on several configurable UI elements:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"label"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": It is used to describe the purpose of the input.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"In some UI contexts, especially when space is limited or when the input is part of a compact layout (search bars, filters, inline forms), the label can be hidden.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"However, hiding the label should only be done if the purpose of the input remains clear thanks to a placeholder or contextual icon","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and if the label is still accessible to screen readers","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Hiding a label is a design choice that must balance visual simplicity and clarity of intent, without compromising inclusiveness or form guidance.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"placeholder"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": if the text of the text input is empty a placeholder provides a hint or guidance inside the field to suggest expected input.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A prefix and a suffix can be added to give more context.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"leading icon"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": it helps indicate the purpose of the input (magnifying glass for search, envelope for email, phone device for phone number).","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Only use a leading icon if it adds clear functional or contextual value.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"trailing action"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": it is used to provide actions related to the field: clear input, toggle password visibility, open a date picker, etc.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Can also indicate status or feedback (error checkmark, loading spinner).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Outlined-style","level":2,"text":"Outlined style"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"By ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"default"}]},{"text":", the input is with a subtle background fill and invisible bottom border, creating a softer and more contained look.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Best suited for dense layouts or to enhance visibility.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"outlined"}]},{"text":", the text input is a minimalist design with a transparent background and a visible stroke outlining the field.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"This style may be interesting for contexts other than form pages:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When inputs need to feel lightweight and unobtrusive","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In a header (search field)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In a selection\/filtering feature in a product catalog","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"code":["   \/\/ An outlined text input","   OUDSTextInput(label: \"Label\", text: $text, isOutlined: true)","","   \/\/ With a localizable and a bundle","   OUDSTextInput(LocalizedStringKey(\"label_wording\"), bundle: Bundle.module, text: $text)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Rounded-layout","level":3,"text":"Rounded layout"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Text input can have rounded layouts to be favored in more emotional, immersive contexts or those tied to specific visual identities.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"For standard or business-oriented journeys, keep the default corners.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"This evolution addresses the need for flexibility in adapting the design to some brand contexts.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"To activate the rounded corner behavior, set to true the ","type":"text"},{"code":"hasRoundedTextInputs","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" values of the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Tuning","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" object","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in your theme configuration (if the theme exposes this property at init).","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Some themes do not have this flexibility like ","type":"text"},{"code":"SoshTheme","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"WireframeTheme","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Status","level":2,"text":"Status"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Five status are proposed for all layouts:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"default (by default)"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": Default neutral appearance, whether empty or filled.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"It allows users to click, focus, and type freely without restrictions.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"error"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": The ","type":"text"},{"code":"error","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" status indicates that the user input does not meet validation rules or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"expected formatting. It provides immediate visual feedback, typically through a red border,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"error icon, and a clear, accessible error message positioned below the input. The error messages replaces the helper text.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"loading"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": The ","type":"text"},{"code":"loading","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" state indicates that the system is processing or retrieving data","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"related to the text entered. A progress indicator appears to inform the user that an action is in progress.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"readOnly"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" :The","type":"text"},{"code":"readOnly","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", lets the text visible but not editable","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"disabled"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": In ","type":"text"},{"code":"disabled","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" status, the field is non-interactive and grayed out to indicate it cannot be changed.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Note the SwiftUI ","type":"text"},{"code":"View.disabled()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ignored.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Helpers","level":2,"text":"Helpers"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Helper text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":":  A supporting text conveys additional information about the input field,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"such as how it will be used. It should ideally only take up a single line, though may wrap","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to multiple lines if required, and be either persistently visible or visible only on focus.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Helper link"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": If the helper text is not sufficient, it’s possible to offer the user","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an additional help link (the link can be external or open a modal).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Accessibility-considerations","level":2,"text":"Accessibility considerations"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"By default no haptics are done by the component for the trailing action.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"However you should think about cases wher you will have to make the devices vibrates.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"You can refer to the ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/developer.apple.com\/design\/human-interface-guidelines\/playing-haptics"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Mandatory-field-indication","level":2,"text":"Mandatory field indication"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If all fields are mandatory (several fields present): display the message “All fields are mandatory” at the top of your formular.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Do not use an asterisk at the end of each field label, nor the word “mandatory.”","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If not all fields are mandatory (several fields present): display the message “All fields marked with an * are mandatory” at the top of your formular.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Use an asterisk (*) at the end of each mandatory field label, and ensures this is well vocalized.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"UI rendering of the asterisk must be done with ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"bold font weight"}]},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"negative content color"}]},{"text":" (red on light backgrounds).","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use the mention “(optional)” at the end of each optional field label. Note that this rule is not systematic, it remains an option, to be used if needed.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If there is only one field in the formular, or if the mandatory nature is obvious (such as login\/password),","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"no mention is necessary since the fields are essential to the formular’s functionality.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Rich-text","level":2,"text":"Rich text"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Rich text can be used for error and helper texts.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Strong text can be used sparingly to highlight key information within the content.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"No other text styles should be used.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Underlined text must not be applied manually (e.g. in error message), as it is commonly associated with hyperlinks and may mislead users.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Code-samples","level":2,"text":"Code samples"},{"code":["    \/\/ The text to display and edit","    @State var text: String = \"\"","","    \/\/ Empty text and no placeholder","    OUDSTextInput(label: \"Email\", text: $text)","","    \/\/ Empty text with placeholder and suffix","    OUDSTextInput(label: \"Email\", text: $text, placeholder: \"firstName.lastName\", suffix: \"@orange.com\")","","    \/\/ Empty text with prefix and suffix","    OUDSTextInput(label: \"Email\", text: $text, prefix: \"Distance\", suffix: \"km\")","","    \/\/ Add a leading icon for more context","    OUDSTextInput(label: \"Email\", text: $text, placeholder: \"firstName.lastName\", suffix: \"@orange.com\",","                  leadingImage: OUDSImage(asset: Image(systemName: \"envelope\")))","","    \/\/ Add a leading icon displayed as raw image (not tinted)","    OUDSTextInput(label: \"Brand\", text: $text,","                  leadingImage: OUDSImage(asset: Image(\"ic_brand\"), renderingMode: .original))","","    \/\/ Flip the leading icon for RTL layouts using OUDSImage.flipped","    OUDSTextInput(label: \"Label\", text: $text,","                  leadingImage: OUDSImage(asset: Image(\"ic_arrow\"), flipped: layoutDirection == .rightToLeft))","","    \/\/ Add a trailing button with local image named \"ic_cross\" for additional action","    let trailingAction = OUDSTextInput.TrailingAction(image: OUDSImage(asset: Image(\"ic_cross\")), actionHint: \"Delete\") { text = \"\" }","    OUDSTextInput(label: \"Email\", text: $text, trailingAction: trailingAction)","","    \/\/ With helper text","    OUDSTextInput(label: \"Email\",","                  text: $text,","                  placeholder: \"firstName.lastName\",","                  suffix: \"@orange.com\",","                  helperText: \"The email will be automatically completed with @orange.com\")","","    \/\/ With helper link","    @Environment(\\.openURL) private var openUrl","","    let helperLink = OUDSTextInput.HelperLink(text: \"Helper Link\") {","       openUrl.callAsFunction(url)","    }","","    OUDSTextInput(label: \"Label\", text: $text, placeholder: \"Placeholder\", helperLink: helperLink)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If you need to flip your leading icon for RTL, use the ","type":"text"},{"code":"flipped","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" property of ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSImage"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"code":["    @Environment(\\.layoutDirection) var layoutDirection","","    OUDSTextInput(label: \"Label\", text: $text,","                  leadingImage: OUDSImage(asset: Image(\"ic_arrow\"), flipped: layoutDirection == .rightToLeft))"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Design-documentation","level":2,"text":"Design documentation"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/r.orange.fr\/r\/S-ouds-doc-text-input"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Themes-rendering","level":2,"text":"Themes rendering"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Orange","level":3,"text":"Orange"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"image","identifier":"component_textInput_Orange"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Orange-Compact","level":3,"text":"Orange Compact"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"image","identifier":"component_textInput_OrangeCompact"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Sosh","level":3,"text":"Sosh"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"image","identifier":"component_textInput_Sosh"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Wireframe","level":3,"text":"Wireframe"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"image","identifier":"component_textInput_Wireframe"}]},{"type":"aside","name":"Version","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"1.4.0 (Figma component design version)"}]}],"style":"note"},{"type":"aside","name":"Since","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"0.20.0"}]}],"style":"note"}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents"]]},"topicSections":[{"title":"Structures","generated":true,"anchor":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSTextInput\/Helperlink","doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSTextInput\/TrailingAction"]},{"title":"Initializers","generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSTextInput\/init(_:tableName:bundle:text:placeholder:prefix:suffix:leadingImage:trailingAction:helperText:helperLink:isOutlined:constrainedMaxWidth:status:)-6fxq4","doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSTextInput\/init(_:tableName:bundle:text:placeholder:pre